Completing [[Slayer]] tasks is the sole way for [[Ironman Mode|Ironmen]] to acquire or upgrade several best-in-slot items, such as the [[abyssal whip]], [[dragon boots]], [[trident of the seas]], [[occult necklace]], and [[dragon hunter lance]]. High-level Slayer can also be an excellent way to earn money through valuable [[High Level Alchemy|alchables]].

[[Duradel]] is generally the best Slayer master to use. [[Konar quo Maten]] should be used for every milestone task for the extra [[Slayer reward point]]s.

Using a [[dwarf multicannon]] is usually not worthwhile for efficient Slayer training on an Ironman due to the time required to make [[steel cannonball]]s, with the exception of [[smoke devil]]s in some cases. Because of this, certain tasks which are decent on a main account, such as [[suqah]]s and [[kalphite]]s, are not worth doing as an Ironman, as they have no notable drops and offer mediocre experience rates without a cannon. Blocking [[suqah]]s and [[kalphite]]s should be one of your first priorities with Slayer points as an Ironman.

For tasks you want to finish quickly (usually when prioritising Slayer points), it is recommended to wear the [[expeditious bracelet]], since it has a 25% chance to treat each kill as 2 kills towards the Slayer task. If you instead want to extend the task, a [[bracelet of slaughter]] will have a 25% chance for a kill to not count towards the Slayer task.

When using Slayer reward points, prioritise blocking and skipping poor tasks over unlocking perks and extensions. Unlock superior Slayer monsters, the [[Slayer helmet]], and the ability to craft [[Slayer ring]]s first. If you use Ranged often, consider unlocking ''[[Slayer Rewards|Broader Fletching]]'' perk early on for the ability to fletch [[broad bolts]].

Unless only focusing on quicker [[Magic]] levels, use [[Combat Options#Defensive 2|defensive casting]] when bursting tasks (such as [[dust devil]]s), since it gives more experience overall. If you are low on [[herb seed]]s, kill normal [[nechryael]] with melee instead of bursting [[greater nechryael]] in the [[Catacombs of Kourend]].

Before you can kill [[abyssal demon]]s for the [[abyssal whip]], train only Strength after you have 75 [[Attack]] (to use [[Arclight]]) and 70 [[Defence]] (to use [[Barrows equipment]]), unless you want to hit combat level 100 sooner to access Duradel. Once you have obtained the abyssal whip, train on the [[Combat Options#Controlled|Controlled style]] until you have 99 Strength, and after that train Attack and Defence. If you have a [[kraken tentacle]], use any excess abyssal whips for an [[abyssal tentacle]].

==Starting off==
The [[natural history quiz]] has no requirements and rewards 1,000 Slayer experience, making for an easy way to reach level 9 Slayer.

To train Slayer efficiently, it is recommended that you begin after reaching 80–90 combat, with reasonable gear.

Recommended skills:

*70+ {{SCP|Attack}}, {{SCP|Strength}} and {{SCP|Defence}}
*{{SCP|Magic|48}} ([[Kourend Castle Teleport]])
*{{SCP|Prayer|43}} ([[Protect from Melee]])
*{{SCP|Herblore|45}} ([[Super attack|super attack potions]]) or {{SCP|Herblore|55}} ([[Super strength|super strength potions]])
*{{SCP|Agility|70}} ([[Taverley Dungeon]] shortcut to [[blue dragon]]s)
*{{SCP|Crafting|27}} for the ability to make [[emerald ring]]s for [[Ring of dueling|rings of dueling]]

Using Ranged for low-level Slayer tasks in general is not recommended due to the poorer damage output of the available weapons and ammunition compared to dragon scimitar. However, some tasks can prove to be difficult or tedious to do without Prayer flicking or use of [[prayer potion]]s, so [[safespot]]ting with Ranged can be a justified option in some cases.

===Point boosting===
{{Main|Slayer reward points#Point boosting}}
Players can utilise [[Turael]] or [[Mazchna]] for point boosting. Mazchna is a viable alternative to Turael, as his tasks reward 6 points per task. Players might consider incorporating Mazchna into every 10th task while Turael skipping, using [[Konar quo Maten]] for every 50th task.  See the main article above for more info.

==== Turael ====
[[File:Turael chathead.png|left]]
When starting Slayer training, the first priority is to block the most common bad tasks while reserving some Slayer points for skipping less common but equally bad tasks. It is therefore optimal to start by boosting Slayer points by using [[Turael]] and doing every 10th task at [[Konar quo Maten]] or the highest level Slayer master you are able to use. While Turael tasks do not give good experience, they are very easy and fast to complete unlike some of the tasks given by higher-level Slayer masters.

Turael can be quickly accessed via the [[games necklace]]'s teleport to [[Burthorpe]]. Wearing heavy armour is not recommended, as you will be running a lot and the monsters you are killing do not deal much damage. Whenever you need to bank, teleport to the Ferox Enclave via a ring of dueling or use the minigame teleport and use the free-for-all portal to reset stats and run energy after banking.

Recommended inventory setup for Turael tasks:
*[[Games necklace]]
*[[Ring of dueling]] for resetting stats at the Ferox Enclave
*2 [[super attack]]s (and [[super strength]]s if not using a dragon battleaxe)
*Runes for teleportation
*[[Ardougne cloak 1]] (or higher) and a [[Dramen staff|dramen]]/[[lunar staff]] for access to [[fairy rings]]
*[[Ectophial]]
*[[Chronicle]]
*A [[Light sources|light source]]
*[[Dragon battleaxe]] or [[dragon dagger]] for special attacks
*Energy potions, antipoison (for cave crawlers and slimes) and some food (optional)

Additional information on Turael's tasks and where they can be done can be found at [[Slayer reward point#Turael boosting]].

Once you have attained enough Slayer points, block these tasks as soon as you can:

*[[Black demon]]
*[[Hellhound]]
*[[Suqah]] (Konar quo Maten does not assign these)
*[[Kalphite (disambiguation)|Kalphite]] (block last, [[Kalphite Worker]]s are reasonably fast to kill)
Once you have these tasks blocked and some spare points for skipping, move on to the highest-level Slayer master you are able to use.

==== Krystilia (Wilderness Slayer) ====
[[File:Krystilia chathead.png|left|frameless|width=127x127]]
Alternatively, doing Wilderness Slayer tasks from [[Krystilia]] is another option for obtaining a good amount of Slayer points due to rewarding significantly more points per completed task than any other master. Krystilia has no requirements, but players should be sufficient enough to survive in the [[Wilderness]] and are strongly recommended to have at least 43 prayer for access to [[Overheads|overhead prayers]]. When doing Wilderness tasks, only risk easily replaceable equipment you are willing to lose, such as monk robes or dragonhide armour. It's important to note that Krystilia can assign tasks of any combat level (Assuming skill and quest requirements are met), making this a potentially less preferable option at lower combat levels due to the chance of being given slow and/or difficult tasks early on. 

Monsters killed for [[Wilderness]] tasks have the chance to drop [[Larran's key]]s, which can be used to open [[Larran's big chest]] for plenty of cash and useful resources like seeds, gems, ores, food and alchables. Slayer monsters within the [[Wilderness Slayer Cave]] have the added bonus of generally increased drop rates compared to their normal counterparts which, when using [[looting bag]]s for an extra 28 inventory slots, make this a high risk but extremely high reward option of training Slayer. Lastly, monsters within the Wilderness can drop [[blighted food]], [[blighted super restore]]s and [[blighted rune sack]]s, all of which can only be used within the Wilderness and are particularly useful for ironmen as they add some level of self-sustainability and reduce the need to obtain these resources yourself.

