The aim for melee equipment is to maximise strength bonus.

Typical low/mid-level gear includes:
*[[Slayer helmet]] [[Slayer helmet (i)|(i)]]: Can be assembled after purchasing the ''[[Slayer Rewards|Malevolent Masquerade]]'' ability from a Slayer master, costing 400 Slayer reward points. [[Black mask]] can be obtained from [[cave horror]]s.
*Any [[God blessing]]: Can be obtained from [[Treasure Trails]]. Alternatively, [[Rada's blessing 2]] or higher can be used.
* [[Fighter torso]]: Can be obtained from the [[Barbarian Assault]] minigame.
* [[Blood moon chestplate]]/[[Blood moon tassets]] provide the same strength bonus as Bandos gear, but with higher magic defence that is good against magic-based tasks like Bloodvelds, Wyrms, and Aberrant Spectres.
*[[Obsidian platelegs]]: Can be purchased in [[TzHaar-Hur-Zal's Equipment Store]].
*[[Climbing boots]]: Can be bought from [[Tenzing]]. [[Mixed hide boots]] are an alternative with higher defensive bonuses.
*[[Barrows gloves]]: Can be purchased from [[Culinaromancer's Chest]] after completion of [[Recipe for Disaster]].
*[[Amulet of glory]]: [[Dragonstone amulet]] can be made at 80 Crafting and enchanted into an amulet of glory with [[Lvl-5 Enchant]], or obtained from [[dragon impling]]s.
*[[Fire cape]]: Can be obtained as a reward for defeating [[TzTok-Jad]] in the [[Fight Caves]].
*[[Ring of wealth]]: [[Dragonstone ring]] can be made at 55 Crafting, which can be turned into a ring of wealth by Lvl-5 Enchant. Hardcore Ironmen should wear a [[ring of life]] on tasks which they can easily die if they disconnect.
*[[Dragon scimitar]]: Can be purchased from [[Daga]] on [[Ape Atoll]] after completion of [[Monkey Madness I]].
*[[Dragon defender]]: Can be obtained as a rare drop in the basement of the [[Warriors' Guild]] from the [[cyclopes]] that reside there.
*[[Zombie axe]]: Can be made with 70 smithing, after obtaining it in broken form as a rare drop from [[armoured zombie]]s after starting [[Defender of Varrock]].

===Additional equipment===
The [[bonecrusher]] (requiring the [[Morytania Diary#Hard|hard Morytania diary]]), [[ash sanctifier]] (requiring the [[Kourend & Kebos Diary#Hard|hard Kourend & Kebos diary]]), and [[ectoplasmator]] (purchasable from [[Soul Wars]]) can be worthwhile to bring on all tasks where you do not plan to pick up bones or ashes, as they will provide a passive source of [[Prayer]] experience. The bonecrusher specifically will also restore [[Prayer points]] when used within the [[Catacombs of Kourend]], a popular location for many Slayer tasks. [[Bonecrusher]] charges can be easily sustained by the daily bonemeal reward from [[Robin]].

[[Expeditious bracelet]]s and [[Bracelet of slaughter|bracelets of slaughter]] are recommended if desiring to finish an undesirable task quickly or extend a good task, respectively. They do not need to be worn the whole kill, only for the last hit, allowing stat-boosting gloves (such as [[Barrows gloves]] or a [[combat bracelet]]) to be worn for the rest of a kill.

[[Ring of wealth|Rings of wealth]] are a good choice for the ring slot if you have no stat-boosting rings (such as a [[berserker ring]]), as it automatically collects coin drops from monsters.

